    "notes": "A poor capture of a packet that is, on the evidence of the label itself, compliant. None of the six declarations is legibly present in THIS line set: the MRP line was not recognised at all, 'NET QTY:' (line 30) was read without its value, and the manufacturer block came back as licence-number fragments ('Ods, Lic. No. 11221999000261'). With nothing recoverable, min_fields_found=2 is not met and the honest answer is INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE - 'move closer and try again' - not a verdict. The app currently returns ATTENTION with four findings, all false. That is the exact P3 failure the demo exists to avoid, and it is the headline D-3 result. Two specific false positives to kill: commodity_name must not take the INGREDIENTS line (it returned 's (6779%) (rice meal (44%),' at HIGH confidence), and net_quantity must not take '100g' from the nutrition table's 'Per 100 g' - that came from Stage B pairing list-index 30 with 31, which are 1668 px apart in different columns. JUDGEMENT CALL: 'namkeen' from line 8 ('PROPRIETARYFOOD--NAMKEEN(15.1)') is arguably the commodity name and could be expected instead of null. Left null because P3 prefers silence to a value, and one packet is not enough to add a lexicon term."
